:{"input_tokens":5140,"output_tokens":298,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"575cb45b35202f79c14984167932297d0d67852eae710976dce9ddff28564935"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":100543,"output_tokens":1785,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"761e4f915e2dc2f22b1d499b47cd4ff79258afa1a16ae70064abaf6cdb1ce001"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":5068,"output_tokens":267,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"eb790521e61aafa6121bf2095da8228a668420b79eeb09b459c750a68b42e278"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":19262,"output_tokens":885,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"0ff7aacabd98971a8c2df3cedcc1c4520b7838a777e0a0bcec734f45e684d549"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":14844,"output_tokens":530,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"02aea7c8715874de80d92a9eb505fc6ac7e6f2ec6cfdb55f1694c7d977728aeb"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":21611,"output_tokens":670,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"ba98e4578d211e47363864c2ba3b9ded12f995445e8285d95c2b89e987c07055"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":18797,"output_tokens":846,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"cc6388fe854bdc47e60028a2f6ad74b12dbda375e4e9a0dad950cf0918fd457c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:E4","usage":{"input_tokens":172280,"output_tokens":4469,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct the root-cause: current _slim (sidecar.py:664) emits norm_id UNCONDITIONALLY via norm_id() — identify and cite the ACTUAL source of norm_id-less committed findings (e.g. an older sidecar schema version) rather than attributing it to current _slim's field-select behavior.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0056,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["sidecar.py:664 `\"norm_id\": norm_id(f),` inside `_slim` — unconditional, not gated on tier","sidecar.py:311-319 `def norm_id(finding)` returns `'n' + sha256(...)[:16]` for any input; never None, never omitted","The plan quotes the crashing line correctly (fixture_selection.py:234) but mis-attributes WHY a norm_id key would be absent"],"finding":"The plan's central premise — that plan-review's _slim 'emits norm_id only for normalized (LLM) findings and OMITS it for deterministic (tier: DET) findings' — is refuted by the current code. sidecar.py line 664 sets '\"norm_id\": norm_id(f)' UNCONDITIONALLY, and norm_id() (sidecar.py line 311-319) always returns a non-empty string for any finding regardless of tier. The current _slim therefore always emits a norm_id key for DET findings too, so the described mechanism cannot produce the KeyError on any finding written by the current sidecar.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc271148c11db643f","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context section — 'Plan-review's sidecar _slim is a field-SELECT ... emits norm_id only for normalized (LLM) findings and OMITS it for deterministic (tier: DET) findings.'","norm_id":"n22513ef7bb131484","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer trusting the stated mechanism concludes the fix is safe because DET findings 'have no norm_id'; but current DET findings DO carry a norm_id, so the described exclusion also silently drops valid norm-bearing DET findings if the real cause differs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Re-ground the norm_id-omission premise: bug 884d confirms only that DET findings lack a *verification* block — provide a source that actually establishes norm_id-less committed findings (a real corpus query, or the specific historical schema/commit that omitted norm_id).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.75,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Bug 884d description/comment discuss the *verification* block: '53 are tier=\"DET\" ... deterministic detector ... findings that never enter Pass-2, so no verification exists to persist'","884d contrasts plan-review's `_slim` (field-selection, must name `verification` explicitly) with code-review's `_with_norm_ids` field-spread — the discriminator is `verification`, not `norm_id`","Nothing in 884d states DET findings lack a norm_id key"],"finding":"The plan cites bug 884d-ece3-c961-4959 as confirming that _slim omits norm_id for DET findings, but that ticket does not establish this. Ticket 884d confirms _slim is a field-SELECTION and that DET-tier findings legitimately lack a *verification* block — it never discusses norm_id being absent for DET findings. The citation supports the 'field-SELECT' framing but not the specific 'OMITS norm_id for DET findings' claim it is offered as evidence for.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f492db94e74e358fd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context section — '(confirmed in bug 884d-ece3-c961-4959)'","norm_id":"nb3b296b1992f8fae","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer following the citation to validate the premise finds it addresses verification, not norm_id, and cannot confirm the stated cause"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"748acba84e3e657d","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["13ae2bb1f5be7a2f",2947],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["1a84133a75b70821",2],"ticket_id":["9f63afd942b73df7",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":271324,"cache_write_tokens":137833,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; th